      "id": 1,
      "text": "Buena Vista was founded in 1830, establishing itself as a Georgia frontier town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofbuenavista.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city changed its name from Pea Ridge to Buena Vista to honor Zachary Taylor's victory in the Mexican–American War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buena_Vista%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A devastating fire in 1906 destroyed much of Buena Vista, but brick rebuilding followed shortly thereafter.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buena_Vista%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Buena Vista serves as the county seat of Marion County, hosting the county courthouse.",
